WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Diff, validate and label circuit-tracer circuits. Attribution graphs show where influence flows. circuitkit asks what training changed, whether the features cause the behaviour, and what each feature does.

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.600
circuitkit: three tools on top of circuit-tracer attribution graphs.

3
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.100
Why: in two studies the graph's top features read the behaviour but did not drive it.

4
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:18.600
A five-minute quickstart runs every tool offline: toy model, bundled graphs, cached replies.

5
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.600
Each tool has a guide: the checks, the verdicts and the parameters.

6
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.100
And an API reference. Every code snippet in these docs runs in the test suite.

7
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:41.000
The validator: is a group of graph features a switch or a readout?

8
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:55.000
The graph diff: what did RL change inside Qwen3-1.7B?

9
00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Feature labels: Claude Haiku 5.5 explains each feature from its top examples,

10
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.000
pip install steerlab-circuitkit. Docs, notebooks and the five-minute quickstart: github.com/albertlieyingadrian/steerlab · packages/circuitkit
